    "description": "Vintage-style sterling silver and turquoise jewelry grouping featuring a substantial turquoise statement ring accompanied by a pair of coordinating turquoise sterling silver earrings.\nThe ring features a rounded turquoise cabochon in a raised bezel surrounded by an architectural, fluted silver setting. The shoulders have bold dimensional ribbed detailing that gives the ring a classic Southwestern statement-jewelry appearance. The interior shows age-related surface wear and oxidation consistent with vintage use.\nThe ring measures approximately size 7½ on the photographed mandrel.\nThe coordinating earrings feature round turquoise cabochons with visible natural-looking matrix in smooth sterling silver settings. The reverse sides are visibly stamped “STERLING” along with additional maker/initial markings that appear to include “GIL” and “MW”; please refer to the detailed photographs for the exact marks. The earrings are fitted with post backs.\nPhotographed scale readings include approximately:\nRing: 0.216 oz / approximately 6.135 g\nEarrings: 0.237 oz / approximately 6.740 g\nThe photographs also document the approximate physical dimensions of the earrings against a ruler.\nTurquoise varies naturally between the pieces in tone and matrix, giving the grouping an appealing collected-over-time character. Stone identification is based on appearance and existing context; no gemological testing is represented.\nPre-owned jewelry showing patina, oxidation, scratches, tarnish, and general surface wear consistent with age and previous use. Please review all photographs carefully for exact condition, markings, sizing, stone coloration, and construction.\nCollector/Reseller Note: An appealing grouping for collectors of vintage Southwestern jewelry, sterling silver, turquoise, statement rings, and wearable estate jewelry.",
